// The site's page tree.
// A page is named here by the label doxygen-filter.py gives it, so a label renamed there is renamed here too.
// The order of the blocks is the order of the sidebar; a page named in none of them is published at
// the top level, but AFTER every block, which is why a childless top-level page still needs one.
//
// The list carries no heading: a heading in one of these blocks becomes a section that doxygen files
// in the sidebar under the first child page, pointing back at the parent.
//
// @subpage adds a link to the page it names and makes that page a subpage of this one, both at once.
// The link lands at the top of the parent page, ahead of the markdown the page is rendered from, which
// already lists the same children for a reader on GitHub.
// site.css hides the div to drop that second copy; @internal hides it too and drops the parenting with it.

/**
@page images
*/

/**
@page standalone-scripts
<div class="page-children">
@subpage install-scripts
@subpage check-scripts
</div>
*/

/**
@page guides
<div class="page-children">
@subpage cross-compilation
@subpage coverage
</div>
*/

/**
@page how-to-contribute
<div class="page-children">
@subpage images-validation
@subpage release-process
@subpage release-records
@subpage repository-tooling
@subpage documentation-site
</div>
*/
